# C11 event-host inject — DO NOT APPLY

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Base: origin/cursor/c11-event-source-inject-e504 db5ff40afe5dc15c56c9d299a18165c74707078b
Branch: cursor/c11-event-host-inject-e504

DO NOT APPLY this hunk. Do not edit App/AppSession.swift, App/AppCompositionRoot.swift, or Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj from this branch.

`Core/ProfileOrderEventHost.swift` is the real host. `ProfileOrderEventSourceInjection` stays the caller-held row injection and is not rewritten. WithdrawalSupportLandingView balance (`withdrawal.support.balance`) and stages (`withdrawal.support.notReceived`) stay unchanged.

The host posts `api/registration/info` and, only when that info id equals the opened order, `api/registration/original-event`. It maps a returned row into the existing injection only when the first ORDER id equals the opened order. ProfileOrder fields are not OriginalAuditEvent. A mismatch, a transport failure, or an absent body does not invent an event and does not call /business/audit-log.

## Why the session must pass the host

`profileService` is private on AppSession (around line 2428). `SessionOwnedOrdersView` only has the session. `ProfileService.postOwnedOrderForm(path:id:token:)` now returns the raw form body, and `ProfileOrderEventHost.open` calls it for `api/registration/info` and, only when that info id matches, for `api/registration/original-event`. Passing that host still requires AppSession. This hunk does not add that call.

## Withheld call site

File: `App/AppSession.swift`, beside `ownedOrderReader` (around line 3106).
File: `App/OwnedOrderComposition.swift` `SessionOwnedOrdersView`.
Do not apply.

```swift
func openOwnedOrderOriginalEvent(_ openedOrderID: Int) async -> Int64? {
    guard openedOrderID > 0, let token, AuthRequestBuilder.isValidToken(token) else { return nil }
    guard let profileService else { return nil }
    var host = ProfileOrderEventHost()
    // ProfileService.postOwnedOrderForm returns the response body bytes.
    // Do not decode ProfileOrder. Do not copy title, amount, or member id into OriginalAuditEvent.
    return await host.open(openedOrderID, service: profileService, token: token)
}
```

```
         ProfileOrdersView(reader: session.ownedOrderReader, ticketReader: session.ticketWalletReader)
+            // session.openOwnedOrderOriginalEvent(openedOrderID) supplies the host.
+            // Apply only together with the AppSession method above.
             .id(session.ownedOrderReader.identity)
```

`postOwnedOrderForm(path:id:token:) async throws -> Data?` is a member of ProfileService. It is not a member of AppSession. Until AppSession passes `profileService` into `ProfileOrderEventHost.open`, the orders page keeps its current quiet lookup and this hunk stays unapplied.

